@@ -3,3 +3,10 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## Usage
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` (from `src/index.ts`) returns the value a JSON Pointer
+([RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901)) refers to. It throws if the pointer is malformed or
+does not resolve to a value of the document (including the `-` array token, which names no existing
+element). Run the tests with `npm test`.
